next  level sold my car and I disconnected my  cell phone and broke up with his  longtime girlfriend it wasn't for  nothing though Adrian Brody became the  youngest actor to ever win an Oscar for  best actor at the age of 29. number four  the life of a ballerina is no delicate  dance ask any professional ballet dancer  about their training regime and they'll  let you know it's one of the most  unnatural and physically demanding forms  of entertainment that exists today  Natalie Portman did not shy away from  this While She Was preparing to play  this role in Black Swan taking her  challenge dangerously close to a  Breaking Point either physical or mental  Natalie undertook a sparse diet that  included eating only almonds and carrots  she also began practicing ballet for  eight hours a day started  serious ballet training it was  definitely challenging number five  Hollywood audiences are no strangers to  drastic body Transformations on screen  preparing to play his role in Dallas  Buyers Club this actor found himself  losing 30 pounds the point of being  difficult to recognize it just happens  it's an intuition it's a guttural  response to a character and a script but  what really puts Leto on the list for  taking it too far are his actions when  playing Joker in Suicide Squad Jared  decided to play some unusually cruel and  unsanitary practical jokes on the rest  of the cast and crew while this might be  something that has been tolerated in the  past from actors playing principle roles  Leto's role in Suicide Squad only saw  about 10 minutes of screen time we've  had a lot of fun doing it number six  it's hard to imagine what it would be  like to live with blindness but not for  Ray Charles's biopic actor Jamie Foxx to  prepare for the role and to help make  the performance appear more authentic  fox used prosthetic eyelids that  effectively made him unable to see it  was no easy task as Jaime suffered from  frequent and debilitating panic attacks  that at times threatened to delay the  production of the film number 7. too  pretty or too smelly Holly Berry wanted  the role in Spike Lee's jungle fever so  much that when Lee didn't seem keen on  casting her Holly took it the extra mile  Spike Lee believed that Holly Berry was  too pretty to play the role of a street  woman to show him otherwise Barry delved  deep into the life of a streetwalker  spending time in a real drug den and  giving up bathing for the duration of  shooting the production really got to  shed my physical self that beauty  pageant image number eight it took took  many roles and many nominations for this  actor to finally win an Oscar we can't  help but wonder if after each almost win  this actor felt the need to do something  dramatically different while preparing  for his next role maybe that's what led  the Revenant actor Leonardo DiCaprio to  give up his plant-based food diet and  eat raw bison liver while shooting this  film he even went so far as to sleep  inside real animal carcasses to get a  feeling for the Wilderness survival  experience would not have been the same  experience had we not really been there  in these environments number nine this  actor has a Next Level commitment to  modifying his appearance for pretty much  every role we've seen him perform but  there are a few times where he might  have taken his transformation a little  too far one might be the time he gained  40 pounds to play the role of Dick  Cheney in Vice or how about the time  Bale lost an alarming 63 pounds for his  role in The Machinist leaving the actor  in a state of health that almost took  his life I mean I remember at the time  it was like not the smart thing to do  number 10 playing The Joker Ledger has  been credited with making this villain  memorable to his credit this probably  had something to do with the mental and  physical transformation that ledger took  on in playing this character but at what  cost we might even say that Heath Ledger  pushed himself farther for the role of  Joker than he had for any of his other  roles with Heath's dedication to this  transformation came sleep deprivation  exhaustion and heavy use of a sleep  medication while preparing to play The  Joker Heath Ledger isolated himself from  the rest of the World by hiding away in  a hotel for six weeks Ledger's  transformation into the Joker was so  immersive that it was hard to tell where  the character ended and the person began  while it might not be directly related  some view Heath's preparation for this  role as the cause of a mental health  breakdown that ultimately claimed his  life whether that's the case or not  Heath Ledger's death meant a huge blow  to the entertainment industry his work  as the Joker was the final chapter of  his beloved and short acting career  number 11. Heath Ledger wasn't the only  actor to struggle with the role of the  Joker the origin story for this  character saw Joaquin Phoenix starring  in the title role of the Joker striving  for a more authentic portrayal of this  downtrodden character Phoenix lost 50  pounds for the role in the beginning  you're exhausted Joaquin made this  transformation so quickly and  drastically that maintaining the weight  loss took a bigger toll the actor  developed an eating disorder while  shooting this film he became obsessed  with his body weight and after shooting  ended he struggled to get back to a  healthy mindset regarding food and  fitness we realized that it was wrong it  was just the the wrong approach number  12. this actor has been both praised and  feared for this role playing the title  role in Monster the Jeffrey Dahmer story  Evan Peters receives compliments for his  uncanny portrayal of the killer as well  as criticism saying that the retelling  of this story is too sensitive for  viewers while getting the bad guy  feeling right might be what an actor  strives for in a role the preparation  and emotional Fallout can be enough to  make one want to turn down the offer  Peters has said that taking on this role  was one of the hardest things he will  ever have to do in his career and that  in order to do so he was going to have  to go to really dark places and stay  there for an extended period of time the  Jeffrey Dahmer story is is so much  bigger than than just him for Better or  For Worse these esteemed actors seem to  find a way to challenge themselves in  ways we'd expect to see more from  Olympians or professional athletes we  know this couldn't be a complete list so  what do you think who did we miss let us  know in the comments below

